{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fnviaxgszikaj2riekxdtmn723nkm2wxk2k74ufun3qtoha4fftq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_012pxtBjuz7X3PcHf1vMTwsW","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-pUpj6k/translated_rust/src/lib.rs","old_string":"/// The `switch` has no `default:` arm and control can fall off the end of the\n/// function, which is undefined behaviour in C.  This bug is intentionally NOT\n/// fixed.  The `-O3` artifact built from `c_src` reaches its epilogue with\n/// `%rax` still holding the value moved there in the prologue (`mov %rdi,%rax`,\n/// i.e. the `B` argument, since the 20-byte `c2Ray A` is passed in memory), so\n/// an out-of-range `typeB` yields the low 32 bits of `B` as the return value.\n/// That is reproduced here.","new_string":"/// The `switch` has no `default:` arm and control can fall off the end of the\n/// function, which is undefined behaviour in C.  This bug is intentionally NOT\n/// \"fixed\"; the value produced for an out-of-range `typeB` is, however, not\n/// reproducible, because it differs between builds of the very same C source:\n///\n/// * `-O2`/`-O3`: the prologue is `mov %rdi,%rax`, so the epilogue returns the\n///   low 32 bits of the `B` pointer (the 20-byte `c2Ray A` is passed in memory,\n///   so `B` is the first register argument, `%rdi`).\n/// * `-O0` (what CMake produces by default, i.e. `c_src/build/…so`): nothing on\n///   that path writes `%rax` at all, so the function returns whatever the\n///   *caller* happened to leave in `%rax` — not a function of the arguments.\n///\n/// This translation reproduces the `-O2`/`-O3` artifact.  What both builds do\n/// agree on, and what the differential tests assert, is that `*out` is left\n/// untouched and that no dereference happens.  See `ERRORS.md` row E23."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":