{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_qyzly4esozkq5kpj6hzezcw5z535njz74et7hexx6exyhi7eaw3q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All verification phases pass. Final summary of the work:\n\n## Result\n\n**8 real divergences found and fixed in the Rust translation** — all in NaN/UB-corner behaviour that happy-path tests miss. I derived the ground truth by disassembling the reference C artifact (`objdump -d`) instruction by instruction, because x86 SSE returns the *destination* operand when both operands are NaN, and gcc commutes operands relative to the C source text:\n\n| # | function | bug | fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `c2Add` | assumed `a` is the SSE destination | `-O0` puts **`b`** in the destination |\n| 2 | `c2Mulvs` | assumed the scalar `b` is destination | **`a.x`/`a.y`** is the destination |\n| 3 | `c2Dot` | `fadd(p1, p2)` | second product is the destination: `fadd(p2, p1)`, `p2 = b.y*a.y` |\n| 4 | `c2MulmvT` | same as `c2Dot` | same fix, both lanes |\n| 5 | `c2SignedDistPointToPlane_OneDimensional` | hand-folded to `p-d`/`d-p` | `-O0` does **not** inline or fold: real `fsub(fmul(p,n), fmul(d,n))` (`p * -1.0f != -p` for NaN `p`) |\n| 6 | `c2RayToPlane_OneDimensional` | `fmul(db, da)` | `fmul(da, db)` |\n| 7 | `c2RaytoAABB` + `c2RaytoCapsule` | `out->t = fmul(t, A.t)` | `A.t` is the destination: `fmul(A.t, t)` |\n| 8 | `Cargo.toml` dev profile | `ub_checks` turned a NULL-deref into `SIGABRT` | `debug-assertions=false` → `SIGSEGV`, matching C |\n\n## Verification artifacts (all in `translated_rust/`)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 22/22 exported symbols identical (`nm -D` diff empty, dev + release); the 2 `static inline` C functions correctly stay *unexported*.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 68 configuration rows, all passing; plus **gcov proof**: 100 % of C branches evaluated, 100 % of calls, 99.53 % of lines. The one uncovered line (`da*db > 0 → return 1.0f`) is **provably dead code**, with a proof and a 631 608-plane counterexample search.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 36 rejection rows, all with passing differential tests (incl. 8 SIGSEGV-parity comparisons run in child processes, out-of-range `C2_TYPE` enums, misaligned/NULL `out`).\n- **11 test files / 76 test functions / ≈6.5 M bit-exact comparisons**, all via `libloading` on both `.so`s.\n- **Scripts**: `run_diff_tests.sh`, `check_all_features.sh` (power set of `[features]` — exactly one combination, × dev/release), `audit_rows.py` (row↔test traceability audit).\n\n## Two findings worth flagging\n\n1. **The C's own NaN payloads are optimization-level dependent.** `-O0` (the CMake default, i.e. the specified reference) and `-O2`/`-O3` builds of the same `lib.c` disagree on ~9–11 % of both-NaN inputs. No implementation can match both; I match the specified reference build, and verified the translation matches **all** C builds for every non-NaN input.\n2. **`c2CastRay`'s out-of-range `typeB` return value is unreproducible.** At `-O0` it returns the caller's leftover `%rax`; at `-O2` the low 32 bits of `B`. The tests assert only the defined part (`*out` untouched, no fault); this is documented in `ERRORS.md` E23 and in the code.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified (only the `build/` directory the task told me to create)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":834,"cache_read_input_tokens":346415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":834,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f1f401b-82e5-4f2d-882b-528881f517ee","uuid":"466db925-4dba-40bf-8ef3-419e6f202aa9","timestamp":"2026-08-20T10:29:00.260Z"}
